url: "https://shuyaogao.github.io/four-player-doudizhu-rl/"
abstract: >-
  A browser-only teaching demo (AI Teaching Demos): a browser-only teaching demo of two-deck four-player DouDizhu (one landlord vs three peasants). The full rule engine runs in JavaScript and is checked move-by-move against the Python engine. A live "brain panel" shows how a Deep Monte Carlo (DMC) Q-network scores every legal move, with real activations computed from float16 weights; a rule panel explains the greedy baseline. Honest result: this DMC model is weaker than random play, so it is presented as an example of an under-trained network.
keywords:
  - course-demo
  - reinforcement-learning
  - doudizhu
  - card-game
